---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import NewTabIcon from '../components/site/NewTabIcon.astro';
import { newTab } from '../components/site/links';

const CONTACT = 'hello@arkeep.io';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy policy · Arkeep"
  description="What data the arkeep.io website handles when you visit it, who processes it and how to exercise your rights."
>
  <article class="legal wrap" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 id="privacy-title" class="display-lg">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-15">15 October 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <p class="intro">
      arkeep.io sets no cookies, shows no ads and does not track you across sites. This page lists the little data
      that does get handled when you visit, and why.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The data controller is Filippo Crotti, Italy, maintainer of the Arkeep open-source project. For anything about
      this policy or your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
    <p>
      The website at arkeep.io, documentation included, and the anonymous telemetry endpoint at telemetry.arkeep.io.
      The Arkeep software itself runs on your own machines: your backups, credentials and settings never reach us.
    </p>

    <h2>When you visit the site</h2>
    <h3>Hosting</h3>
    <p>
      The site is served by Cloudflare, Inc. To deliver and protect it, Cloudflare processes technical data of each
      request: IP address, browser user agent, requested page and time. Request logs are kept for a few days (at most
      7) for troubleshooting, then deleted. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in running a working, secure website
      (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h3>Visitor statistics</h3>
    <p>
      We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views. It sets no cookies, does not fingerprint your device and
      does not follow you to other sites. We only see aggregate figures such as page views, referring sites, countries
      and device types. Legal basis: legitimate interest in knowing which pages are useful (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h3>GitHub release and star count</h3>
    <p>
      Pages show the latest Arkeep release and the project’s GitHub star count. To keep them current, your browser
      asks the public GitHub API (api.github.com) for these numbers, so GitHub, Inc. receives your IP address and
      user agent. No GitHub account or login is involved. See the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" {...newTab()}>GitHub privacy statement</a>.
      Blocking the request does no harm: the page falls back to the values baked in when it was built. Legal basis:
      legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h3>Links to other sites</h3>
    <p>
      Links to GitHub, Docker Hub and other services take you to sites with their own privacy policies. Nothing is
      loaded from them until you click.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>The site sets no cookies. It keeps two small entries in your browser’s local storage, which never leave your device:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>starlight-theme</code>: the light or dark theme you picked.</li>
      <li><code>arkeep:github</code>: the last release and star count fetched from GitHub, reused for five minutes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Both only serve features you see on the page, so no consent is needed. Clearing site data in your browser removes them.</p>

    <h2>Arkeep telemetry</h2>
    <p>
      An Arkeep server can send a daily anonymous ping to telemetry.arkeep.io: a random instance ID, the Arkeep
      version, the operating system and the number of agents and policies. No IP address, hostname or personal data is
      stored with it, and each record expires after 48 hours. As with the website, Cloudflare processes the request’s IP
      address to deliver it. Details, and how to turn telemetry off, are in the
      <a href="/docs/reference/telemetry/" {...newTab()}>telemetry docs<NewTabIcon /></a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to {CONTACT}, the message is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to a mailbox hosted by Google.
      We use your address and message only to reply, and delete the conversation when it is no longer needed. Legal
      basis: your request (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Transfers outside the EU</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare, GitHub and Google are based in the United States. They are certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy
      Framework and also rely on the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>No advertising, no profiling, no automated decisions about you, and no selling or sharing of data with anyone else.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask for access to, correction or deletion of your data, restrict or object to its
      processing, and receive it in a portable format. Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. Since almost
      everything above is aggregate or short-lived, we may simply hold nothing that identifies you. You can also lodge a
      complaint with the Italian data protection authority,
      <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/" {...newTab()}>Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a>, or with the authority
      where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If what the site does changes, this page changes with it, and the date at the top moves.</p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: calc(68ch + 2 * var(--gutter)); padding-block: var(--space-xxl) 0; }
  header { display: grid; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl); }
  .updated { color: var(--body); font-size: 14px; }
  .intro { font-size: 1.125rem; }
  h2 { margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-sm); font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
  h3 { margin: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-xs); font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; }
  p, li { line-height: 1.65; }
  p + p { margin-top: var(--space-sm); }
  ul { margin: var(--space-sm) 0; padding-left: 1.25em; display: grid; gap: var(--space-xs); }
  a { color: var(--text-link); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
